data.reasoningText:
The `available` field is `undefined` when `availableQuantity` is not provided in the decision. Looking at the cart code:

```typescript
const available = decision.availableQuantity;
if (!decision.available || (available !== undefined && available < line.quantity)) {
  throw new InventoryError(
    decision.reason ??
      `insufficient stock for ${line.product.id}: requested ${line.quantity}, available ${available ?? 0}`,
    line.product.id,
    line.quantity,
    available,  // This is undefined when availableQuantity is not provided
  );
}
```

The issue is that `available` gets passed to the `InventoryError` constructor as `undefined`, even though the error message uses `?? 0` to provide a fallback. I need to apply the same fallback to the constructor argument itself.

